P0 TRANSPARENCY REVIEW

Current src/qp/transparency/log.ts MUST NOT be production infrastructure.

Problems:
- calls itself CT-style but uses a custom padded Merkle tree
- leaf/node hashing is not RFC6962-compatible
- getConsistencyProof() literally returns path: []
- no consistency-proof verifier
- in-memory entries only
- no crash recovery / atomic sequencing
- no anti-equivocation witness
- custom "size:root:timestamp" signed tree head rather than
interoperable checkpoint
- therefore it cannot prove append-only history.

DO NOT PATCH THIS TOY LOG.

Exact production replacement:
https://github.com/transparency-dev/tessera
Current release researched: v1.0.4.
Tessera is the modern transparency.dev implementation built around
tiled transparency logs and production storage personalities.

Standards/components:
- C2SP tlog-tiles:
  https://c2sp.org/tlog-tiles
- C2SP tlog-checkpoint:
  https://c2sp.org/tlog-checkpoint
- C2SP tlog-proof:
  https://c2sp.org/tlog-proof
- C2SP witness:
  https://c2sp.org/tlog-witness
- C2SP trust policy:
  https://c2sp.org/tlog-policy
Libraries:
https://github.com/transparency-dev/formats
https://github.com/transparency-dev/witness

Architecture:
PMail/Privately does NOT expose private evidence to the log.

private run/evidence
  -> QP semantic replay
  -> signed Agent Receipt
  -> run_commitment =3D SHA256(domain || canonical signed receipt/public
commitment)
  -> Tessera append
  -> C2SP checkpoint
  -> inclusion proof
  -> witness cosignatures
  -> portable PrivatelyRunProof

The public tlog entry should contain opaque commitment +
protocol/version metadata only.
NEVER put:
- XMR address/tx metadata
- phone number
- SimpleX address/message
- prompt
- IP
- API credential
- raw evidence
in the public log.

Deploy Tessera as a sidecar/service, not ported into TypeScript.
For local dev: POSIX personality is acceptable.
For production: choose a durable supported backend (S3/GCS/MySQL
depending deployment) and pin container digest/release.

Witnessing:
- run at least two separately hosted witnesses before claiming anti-equivoc=
ation
- configure C2SP tlog-policy quorum
- checkpoint must be considered production-valid only if log signature
+ configured witness quorum verify
- a single PMail-controlled log key is NOT enough to claim split-view
resistance.
- witness state must persist atomically.

SCITT
IETF RFC 9943 (June 2026) is now a Proposed Standard:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9943.html
Use its architecture vocabulary:
Statement -> Signed Statement -> Transparency Service registration ->
Receipt / Transparent Statement.
Do not necessarily implement full SCITT API now, but design
RunStatement/TLogProof so mapping is possible.
The current SCITT Reference API draft is:
draft-ietf-scitt-scrapi-11.
This gives us a standards-aligned path rather than inventing
=E2=80=9CPrivately blockchain.=E2=80=9D

FRONTIER RESEARCH =E2=80=94 implement only what is mature now

1. arXiv:2605.03213
=E2=80=9CWhen Agents Handle Secrets: A Survey of Confidential Computing for=
 Agentic AI=E2=80=9D
Forough, Kogias, Haddadi, May 2026.
Key actionable point: agent systems add tool/memory/delegation threat
surfaces; TEEs + remote attestation help, but compound attestation
across multi-hop agent chains remains an open challenge.
ACTION:
- each runtime/tool hop gets its own attestation/evidence root
- final RunStatement commits to an AttestationGraph root
- never claim one TEE quote proves the entire distributed run.

2. arXiv:2512.14737
=E2=80=9CZero-Knowledge Audit for Internet of Agents: Privacy-Preserving
Communication Verification with MCP=E2=80=9D
Implements Circom-based private communication auditing.
ACTION LATER:
- reproduce their code/benchmarks first
- candidate for proving predicates over committed private messages
(format/usage/billing) without revealing message content
- DO NOT put ZK into MVP trust base until reproduced and independently test=
ed.

3. arXiv:2510.12469
=E2=80=9CProof of Cloud: Data Center Execution Assurance for Confidential V=
Ms=E2=80=9D
Shows conventional CVM attestation does not prove all
physical-host/location assumptions and proposes vTPM/TPM binding.
ACTION:
- privacy class must distinguish TEE_ATTESTED from PHYSICAL_ORIGIN_ATTESTED
- do not claim dstack quote proves provider physical location or
defeats physical attack threat model.

4. arXiv:2503.14611
=E2=80=9CTransparent Attested DNS for Confidential Computing Services=E2=80=
=9D
Combines attestation with DNSSEC/DANE/ACME/CT-style transparency.
ACTION:
- if Privately later exposes a clearnet domain, bind service key +
expected runtime policy/measurement into an attested service identity
and transparency record
- onion service already has self-authenticating address semantics, so
do not force DNS into ANON_CORE.

IMPORTANT conceptual rule:
TLOG PROVES: commitment existed in an append-only witnessed history.
OBSIGNA PROVES: issuer signed exact receipt.
TEE PROVES: measured protected runtime produced/bound key/evidence.
QP PROVES: exact semantic claim is justified from admissible evidence.
None substitutes for another.

Remove/demote:
src/qp/transparency/log.ts
src/qp/transparency/verifier.ts
from production exports once Tessera adapter exists.
Keep only unit-test reference if useful, renamed dev-toy-log.ts.

Acceptance:
- Tessera real process starts
- append opaque run root
- fetch checkpoint
- verify entry inclusion offline
- append second batch
- witness verifies consistency and cosigns
- offline verifier checks inclusion + checkpoint + witness quorum
- restart Tessera/storage and proof still verifies
- attempting alternative inconsistent tree is rejected by witness
- raw private evidence absent from all tlog HTTP assets.
